  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Documentation and Stabilization of the 15th-Century Royal Court at Tibl</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support the documentation of Gurunsi architecture of the Royal Court in Tibl. Once the official residence of the chief of Tibl, the court remains central in the civic and spiritual lives of the Kassena people and contains the regions finest examples of decorated earthen architecture. This project addresses serious flood damage to the site and includes the documentation of building materials and techniques and the development and implementation of a sustainable preservation plan.</narrative>
  </description>
